' S-601 (2026-10-17): the CALL statement with a method of the current class. `CALL Yaz()` (bare, = CALL ME.Yaz()), `CALL ME.Yaz()`,
' `CALL THIS.Yaz()` and `CALL x.Yaz()` are the same call as `Yaz()` / `ME.Yaz()` / `x.Yaz()`. The parser used to take the bare form for a
' global SUB (AST "unsupported call YAZ", MIR "no bound implementation", native "neither a known runtime call nor a function").
CLASS Kutu
    PUBLIC
    DIM v AS I32
    METHOD Yaz()
        PRINT v
    END METHOD
    METHOD Ac()
        v = 4
        CALL Yaz()
        Yaz()
        CALL ME.Yaz()
        CALL THIS.Yaz()
        ME.Yaz()
    END METHOD
END CLASS
DIM x AS Kutu = NEW Kutu()
x.Ac()
CALL x.Yaz()
x.Yaz()
